Vehicle - a program for enforcing neural network specifications

Usage: vehicle [-v|--version] [--logging ARG] [--loggingPass ARG] 
               [--no-warnings] [-j|--json] [COMMAND]

Available options:
  -v,--version             Show version information.
  --logging ARG            Sets the level of detail in the logs if the --log argument has been passed. Supported options: 
                             * NoDetail
                             * MinDetail
                             * MidDetail
                             * MaxDetail
                            (default: NoDetail)
  --loggingPass ARG        Sets which compiler pass logging is enabled for. Supported options: 
                             * Scoping
                             * Typing
                             * Solver
                             * ITP
                             * LossBounds
                             * LossLogic
                             * LossQuantifierLifting
                             * TypingSubsystem
                             * Verification
  --no-warnings            Suppress the printing of warnings.
  -j,--json                Output the program as JSON instead of text.
  -h,--help                Show this help text

Available commands:
  typecheck                Type-check a .vcl specification file.
  compile                  Compile a .vcl specification file.
  verify                   Verify whether properties in a .vcl specification
                           file are true or false.
  validate                 Validate a verification result to check whether it
                           still holds.
  export                   Export a.vcl specification file to an interactive
                           theorem prover.
  list                     List entities for a .vcl specification file.
